{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1397069-first-14th-generation","id":1397069,"title":"First 14th Generation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-17T05:48:27-07:00","id":1397069,"title":"First 14th Generation","content":"When came up actually the first 14th Generation Cainites? Because in V20 it is said that they are relativ young and where first created in the last five years. My problem is that with the way V20 whas written the last five years be anything from 1985-2006. Okay 2006 will it not be with BJD saying that Vampires of the 16th Generation where created within less then a year which makes it year 2004 so the 14th Generation need to be still latest with 2000 in the last millennium. So can anyone help me at which date now so soon came up the 14th and the 15th generations for the first time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T08:47:31-07:00","id":1397099,"title":"","content":"IIRC in older editions it was even possible to have them in DA:Vampire. If we go with the pre Gehenna cronology they began to appear right before the end of the century and were one of the signs of the impending catastrophe. I'd keep it that way but obviously downplay the &quot;end times&quot; aspect... because Gehenna didn't happen after all, so all the escatological millenarism was obviously wrong... right?<br /> <br /> :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T09:12:21-07:00","id":1397101,"title":"","content":"I just tried to see if Time of Thin-Bloods is given anything, there it is said on page 85 in the german version under Dhampire, Children of the Undead in characterconcept, that the Thin-Bloods came up in the last 20 years. About 14th Generation during Dark Ages, the only thing I found out in DAV20 that the 13th generation is new there. So if we assume that they just mixed up 14th and 15th generation I would say first 14th Generation would be 1979 and first 15th generation 1986+ I begin to think that it is with intention left in the dark when in between the 15th generation came up so you can justify adulescent Dhampires and with this leaving in the dark there is this confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T09:23:44-07:00","id":1397105,"title":"","content":"Given the time scale of active vampirism, the first time a 14th generation vampire was created could have been thousands of years ago.<br /> <br /> However, I think the phenomenon of large numbers of 14th generation vampire happened recently - whenever you want to start the Time of Thin Blood.<br /> <br /> Earlier 14th generation vampires were either lone outliers, or were quickly destroyed at the hands of various enemies. And therefore they did not really &quot;contribute&quot; anything as a setting element. They were an odd rumor. Perhaps Princes and Sires simply never permitted 13th generation vampires to embrace, so if they did it was always illegally and easily denied or forgotten.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is that creating 14th generation vampires simply wasn't possible. Any 13th generation who did so, simply created a corpse. The Curse ended there. Or that they created yet another &quot;13th&quot; generation vampire (in terms of mechanics). But then something changed and now we have 14th generation vampires. Spooky. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Of course, this has its own problems for the setting as well. But it's an option if you want to explain why 14th generation vampires now are a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T16:17:00-07:00","id":1397169,"title":"","content":"I believe Time of Thin Blood established that dhamphirs first appeared around the early 1980s, so 15th generation vampires were probably a relatively new phenomenon at that point. Probably the thinning of the blood would have allowed 14th generation vampires for at least a century earlier possibly as much as a millennium (though perhaps they didn't survive very long until recent times).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T16:30:56-07:00","id":1397403,"title":"","content":"The latest round of them appeared in the late 20th century, but it\u2019s almost certain that they\u2019ve occurred before but that they\u2019ve been killed off by one thing or another (the Inquisition, superstitious elders, actual Gehenna cycles, etc.). A dozen generations over millennia just isn\u2019t that much. This has to have happened before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T19:46:33-07:00","id":1397428,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if you take a cyclical view of things (1st and 2nd esp did and there were mentions of 14th in both) they've happened before. In fact it's entirely possible you could have gotten thin bloods at earlier points within the current cycle. The gist of it (from 1st onwards) is that they're rare to the point of being mythical (of course in the dark ages 13th generations were pretty rare too. I believe one of the DAV books mentioned the 12th were even forbidden from embracing..) You'd only start getting large numbers of them until the 80s-90s (seems like a good starting point) but there's no reason the growth couldn't have been gradual over earlier decades. The idea presented in ToTB was that the thin bloods were a product of over-breeding and the 'curse' became something of a self fufilling prophecy (you made so many vampires and they die in big enough numbers that the oldest and most powerful vampires get awakened and start to cull the herd, so to speak. Sort of a Revelation-Space Inhibitor-type effect going on I suppose.)<br /> <br /> So they can show up at any point in a vampire 'cycle' in at least small numbers, but you're only going to get alot of them towards the 'gehenna' end of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T16:45:32-07:00","id":1398462,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it seems likely they have existed here and there, a small percentage of the vampire population, probably since the period of vampiric diaspora following the fall of the Second City. Possibly earlier, if we assume the prophecies concerning the time of thinblood weren't so much a magical vision, as a well-informed prediction of what happens when vampires breed too quickly for their own good.<br /> <br /> It is hard for me to imagine that thin-bloods didn't crop up in certain circumstances, such as:<ul><li>The massive expansion of Clan Cappadocian, which had 12000 members converge for the Feast of Folly.</li> <li>The early establishment of Clan Tremere. Surely, as part of their experimentation with their new vampiric powers, they tested how far the generations could reproduce. If for no other reason than to calibrate Path of Blood 1.</li> <li>The period following the Fall of Rome up to the early modern era, when DAV would have us believe a vampire:human ratio of about 1:1000.</li> <li>The Anarch Revolt. Are you going to be the one to go tell that pack of 13th gen vampires they aren't allowed to embrace anybody?</li> <li>The whole existence of the Sabbat. Mass embraces, by definition, imply lax requirements for siring.</li> </ul><br /> Not to get all Marxian about it, but the main difference in the modern era is thin-blooded vampires attaining a degree of class consciousness around their generation. Until recently, 14th gens existed as notable aberrations and curious individuals. At some point after World War 2, they reached a critical mass where they became aware of one another's existence, while other vampires couldn't help notice them as something other than an odd footnote to Cainite history. This has led to unified action regarding 14th gens, both on their own part and on the part of others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}